<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icf978d5f4a91fc905380ce8d73f6c4950bd907e0" commit="5f75bc350b19154c9a3637829a1e0e38df311bc4" commit_message="dut: Move existing DUT API to &quot;dut.link&quot; - link layer for talking to DUT.  From the new design we want to merge modules &quot;system&quot;, &quot;board&quot;, and &quot;dut&quot; into single hierarchy object. This is the first step of moving existing &quot;cros.factory.test.dut&quot; into &quot;dut_link&quot; layer.  To allow extending more new links easily and integration with board and system, the layout is also revised to follow the design of Board. Now we have a cros.factory.test.dut.link that contains the base class &quot;DUTLink&quot;, with sub-classed implementations in cros.factory.test.dut.links. There is an 'utils' module that provides instance factory (Create).  The class names are also changed to follow Python coding style (keep all-upper case for well-known abbreviations instead of using CamelCase).  BUG=chromium:557573 TEST=make test  Change-Id: Icf978d5f4a91fc905380ce8d73f6c4950bd907e0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/318070 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="318070" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/70/318070/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2f1cfd56a426c950b11eb8944912c0399fd5b27a" commit="3cfbd99657e3c593454ff19f7fdd18fef7982e34" commit_message="dut: New DUTBoard, DUTProperty and DUTComponent.  To run factory software on different platforms we need the system-related modules to be extensible for different platforms using various communication ways. To do that we need to apply the cros.factory.test.dut.link on all system modules instead of doing I/O locally.  This commit extends cros.factory.test.dut to support various system functions.   - pytests should access DUT functions using self.dut.   - The self.dut is an instance of cros.factory.test.dut.board.DUTBoard.   - To access dut you can use       self.dut.Call(..)      self.dut.ReadFile(...)      self.dut.some_component.DoSomething()   - The system functions should be implemented in a DUTComponent. For example,       class Power(DUTComponent):        def DoSomething(self):          pass   - To create a new board with customization, inherit DUTBoard and put in boards    folder then override the properties in your own component class with    @DUTProperty. For example:       class MyPower(Power):        def DoSomething(self):          pas       class MyBoard(DUTBoard):        @DUTProperty        def power:          return MyPower()  To prevent confusion, the new DUT based board environment string has been changed from CROS_FACTORY_BOARD_CLASS to CROS_FACTORY_DUT_BOARD_CLASS, so devices using old setup (and old board implementations) will fall back to DUTBoard instead of crash accidentally (due to argument number difference in init function).  BUG=chromium:557573 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I2f1cfd56a426c950b11eb8944912c0399fd5b27a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/318071 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="318071" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/71/318071/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie81a74e7c815071e84eda8c3a0e5f27e6c45852e" commit="f9737e0a8a3bf57ed9388877d5eb2dd50f0719b7" commit_message="dut: Add DUTLink.IsLocal API.  Some tests may need to do different things if they are running locally on DUT, especially reboot or shutdown related tests. Some system modules can also benefit by using native Python modules (tempfile, glob, ...) to speed up.  To support that, we want to add a new IsLocal API so a DUT link can clearly identify itself for supporting local functions.  We don't rely on detecting link type &quot;isinstance(link, LocalLink)&quot; because there may be proxy or dummy links in future that are actually also running locally.  BUG=chromium:557573 TEST=make test  Change-Id: Ie81a74e7c815071e84eda8c3a0e5f27e6c45852e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/318113 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="318113" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/13/318113/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia4c7e01a718d7f09f04ce633a6c5165e84d0ce90" commit="51f738743e041a40826d9f33a84f2450f3d507eb" commit_message="dut: Add DUT-aware 'Power' component to replace system.power.  Power is the first component we have migrated from system.Board. All pytests are now calling self.dut.power instead of GetBoard(dut).power, or the board APIs.  BUG=chromium:557573 TEST=make test  Change-Id: Ia4c7e01a718d7f09f04ce633a6c5165e84d0ce90 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317961 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317961" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="13" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/61/317961/13" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ia625abf49118e959ab92630213bd1efb4c6c14a7" commit="066fd3e9d450e63498b14155d64d214188953014" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Input: elan_i2c - set input device's vendor and product IDs  Previously the &quot;vendor&quot; and &quot;product&quot; IDs for the elan_i2c driver simply reported 0000.  This patch modifies the elan_i2c driver to include the Elan vendor ID and the touchpad's product id under input/input*/{vendor,product}.  Specifically, this is to allow us to apply a generic Elan gestures config that will apply to all Elan touchpads on ChromeOS.  These configs  match to input devices in various ways, but one major way is by matching on vendor ID.  Adding this patch allows the default Elan touchpad config to be applied to Elan touchpads in this kernel by matching on devices that have vendor ID 04f3.  Note that product ID is also available via custom sysfs entry &quot;product_id&quot; as well.  BUG=chromium:569720 TEST=manually built and installed on a Chromebook with the 3.14 kernel and an Elan touchpad.  Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 3eab4588c958205451fd80dfd219955c5e91c18b)  Change-Id: Ia625abf49118e959ab92630213bd1efb4c6c14a7 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317974 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317974" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/74/317974/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I59565c4dcf991ea5fbb4112956d3ef29fcab16d5" commit="553a14f3865ff2040254b88dce7c87061272555c" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Input: elan_i2c - set input device's vendor and product IDs  Previously the &quot;vendor&quot; and &quot;product&quot; IDs for the elan_i2c driver simply reported 0000.  This patch modifies the elan_i2c driver to include the Elan vendor ID and the touchpad's product id under input/input*/{vendor,product}.  Specifically, this is to allow us to apply a generic Elan gestures config that will apply to all Elan touchpads on ChromeOS.  These configs  match to input devices in various ways, but one major way is by matching on vendor ID.  Adding this patch allows the default Elan touchpad config to be applied to Elan touchpads in this kernel by matching on devices that have vendor ID 04f3.  Note that product ID is also available via custom sysfs entry &quot;product_id&quot; as well.  BUG=chromium:569720 TEST=manually built and installed on a Chromebook with the 3.18 kernel and an Elan touchpad.  Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 3eab4588c958205451fd80dfd219955c5e91c18b)  Change-Id: I59565c4dcf991ea5fbb4112956d3ef29fcab16d5 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317973 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317973" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/317973/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic1fb3c787fdcbc7e87144056dfa22087e886db47" commit="761525c742a89214bc708509ecbe8540a277b62c" commit_message="Add job retry to audio tests  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Ic1fb3c787fdcbc7e87144056dfa22087e886db47 Reviewed-on: ht